#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/major/bind.xml:540
#, xml-text
msgid "Testing BIND"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/major/bind.xml:543
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Test out the new <application>BIND</application> 9 installation.  First "
"query the local host address with <command>dig</command>:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/major/bind.xml:547
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>dig -x 127.0.0.1</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/major/bind.xml:550
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now try an external name lookup, taking note of the speed difference in "
"repeated lookups due to the caching. Run the <command>dig</command> command "
"twice on the same address:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/major/bind.xml:555
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>dig www.&lfs-domainname; &amp;&amp;\n"
"dig www.&lfs-domainname;</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/major/bind.xml:559
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You can see almost instantaneous results with the named caching lookups. "
"Consult the <application>BIND</application> Administrator Reference Manual "
"(see below) for further configuration options."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/major/bind.xml:569
#, xml-text
msgid "Administrator Reference Manual (ARM)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/major/bind.xml:572
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The ARM documentation (do not confuse with the processor architecture)  is "
"included in the source package. The documentation is in .rst format which "
"means that it can be converted in human readable formats if <xref "
"linkend=\"sphinx\"/> is installed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/major/bind.xml:579
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"When <application>BIND</application> is set up, especially if it is going to"
" be operating in a real live scenario, it is <emphasis>highly</emphasis> "
"recommended to consult the ARM documentation. ISC provides an updated set of"
" excellent documentation along with every release so it can be easily viewed"
" and/or downloaded &ndash; so there is no excuse to not read the docs. The "
"formats ISC provides are epub and html at <ulink "
"url=\"https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/&bind-version;/doc/arm/\"/>."
msgstr ""

